{
  "schema_version": "1.0",
  "encounter_id": "01680",
  "segments": [
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0001",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 0.6,
      "end_seconds": 4.18,
      "duration_seconds": 3.58,
      "text": "Morning, doctor. Is this the right room?"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0002",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 5.42,
      "end_seconds": 10.83,
      "duration_seconds": 5.41,
      "text": "Yes, come in and sit down. What brings you here today?"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0003",
      "speaker_id": "person_3",
      "role": "FAMILY_MEMBER",
      "start_seconds": 12.24,
      "end_seconds": 18.08,
      "duration_seconds": 5.84,
      "text": "Hello, doctor. I hope it's alright if I stay in for this."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0004",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 19.06,
      "end_seconds": 23.23,
      "duration_seconds": 4.17,
      "text": "So, yes, that's no problem at all. Please sit."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0005",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 24.77,
      "end_seconds": 26.75,
      "duration_seconds": 1.98,
      "text": "It's a fever, mostly."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0006",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 28.23,
      "end_seconds": 31.23,
      "duration_seconds": 3.0,
      "text": "Has this been going on for long?"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0007",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 33.1,
      "end_seconds": 36.56,
      "duration_seconds": 3.46,
      "text": "Since this morning, that's when it began."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0008",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 37.4,
      "end_seconds": 45.8,
      "duration_seconds": 8.4,
      "text": "Can you describe it a bit more for me? How strong it is, what the pattern is, what helps."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0009",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 47.61,
      "end_seconds": 54.01,
      "duration_seconds": 6.4,
      "text": "I'd give it a three, out of ten. It comes and goes."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0010",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 54.8,
      "end_seconds": 57.64,
      "duration_seconds": 2.84,
      "text": "Is there anything else with it?"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0011",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 58.93,
      "end_seconds": 65.4,
      "duration_seconds": 6.47,
      "text": "A sore throat again goes along with it, most of the time."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0012",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 66.19,
      "end_seconds": 73.36,
      "duration_seconds": 7.17,
      "text": "And the other thing I wanted to mention is that I can't really—"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0013",
      "speaker_id": "person_3",
      "role": "FAMILY_MEMBER",
      "start_seconds": 73.46,
      "end_seconds": 78.63,
      "duration_seconds": 5.17,
      "text": "Tell the doctor about the other thing, that's what worries me."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0014",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 79.98,
      "end_seconds": 96.5,
      "duration_seconds": 16.52,
      "text": "I was getting to that! The sore throat again? That's been for about a week. Yeah, with sore throat again, it's severe, honestly. Yes, swallowing. That makes it worse."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0015",
      "speaker_id": "person_4",
      "role": "NURSE",
      "start_seconds": 98.08,
      "end_seconds": 110.53,
      "duration_seconds": 12.45,
      "text": "Okay, so the vitals from earlier. Temperature is 39.3 degrees, pulse 101, height 156 centimetres, BP is 115 over 67, weight 53 kilos, BMI works out to 21.8."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0016",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 111.86,
      "end_seconds": 112.56,
      "duration_seconds": 0.7,
      "text": "Thanks."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0017",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 115.15,
      "end_seconds": 119.28,
      "duration_seconds": 4.13,
      "text": "I'd like to check you over now, if that's alright."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0018",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 120.58,
      "end_seconds": 123.56,
      "duration_seconds": 2.98,
      "text": "Stay as you are for a moment."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0019",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 137.93,
      "end_seconds": 144.42,
      "duration_seconds": 6.49,
      "text": "The tonsils are large and red with white spots, and the neck glands are tender."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0020",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 146.45,
      "end_seconds": 147.97,
      "duration_seconds": 1.52,
      "text": "Yeah, no problem."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0021",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 151.69,
      "end_seconds": 158.61,
      "duration_seconds": 6.92,
      "text": "All finished, thank you. Have you had any drooling, difficulty breathing or ear pain?"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0022",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 159.14,
      "end_seconds": 171.06,
      "duration_seconds": 11.92,
      "text": "No, no drooling, no difficulty breathing, no ear pain. I did have bad breath at one point, but that went away on its own."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0023",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 173.16,
      "end_seconds": 174.57,
      "duration_seconds": 1.41,
      "text": "How about rash?"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0024",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 175.96,
      "end_seconds": 178.27,
      "duration_seconds": 2.31,
      "text": "No, none, no rash."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0025",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 179.74,
      "end_seconds": 181.7,
      "duration_seconds": 1.96,
      "text": "How's your breathing otherwise?"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0026",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 182.87,
      "end_seconds": 185.34,
      "duration_seconds": 2.47,
      "text": "No, my breathing's been fine."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0027",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 186.83,
      "end_seconds": 188.79,
      "duration_seconds": 1.96,
      "text": "Is there someone at home?"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0028",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 190.21,
      "end_seconds": 194.01,
      "duration_seconds": 3.8,
      "text": "My husband and I live above the shop."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0029",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 195.35,
      "end_seconds": 196.72,
      "duration_seconds": 1.37,
      "text": "Are you active?"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0030",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 197.95,
      "end_seconds": 200.94,
      "duration_seconds": 2.99,
      "text": "I walk the dog every morning."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0031",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 205.84,
      "end_seconds": 211.44,
      "duration_seconds": 5.6,
      "text": "What about your medical history? Just so I get the full picture."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0032",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 212.0,
      "end_seconds": 214.24,
      "duration_seconds": 2.24,
      "text": "I've had asthma, yes."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0033",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 227.67,
      "end_seconds": 231.57,
      "duration_seconds": 3.9,
      "text": "Are you taking anything regularly, including from the pharmacy?"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0034",
      "speaker_id": "person_3",
      "role": "FAMILY_MEMBER",
      "start_seconds": 234.43,
      "end_seconds": 246.18,
      "duration_seconds": 11.75,
      "text": "She takes Foracort inhaler, twice a day for my asthma. She is on paracetamol syrup, 10 ml, every six hours, I give it to her."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0035",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 247.17,
      "end_seconds": 252.66,
      "duration_seconds": 5.49,
      "text": "I had Seretide inhaler at one point, but I'm off it now."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0036",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 253.71,
      "end_seconds": 258.61,
      "duration_seconds": 4.9,
      "text": "Okay, are you allergic to anything? Any allergies to medicines or foods?"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0037",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 259.88,
      "end_seconds": 271.11,
      "duration_seconds": 11.23,
      "text": "Mm, I think I reacted to some antibiotic once, years ago. I don't remember which one, or what happened exactly."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0038",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 288.46,
      "end_seconds": 291.49,
      "duration_seconds": 3.03,
      "text": "Any past operations I should know about?"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0039",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 296.91,
      "end_seconds": 303.02,
      "duration_seconds": 6.11,
      "text": "I had my appendix taken out when I was in my twenties."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0040",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 306.95,
      "end_seconds": 315.42,
      "duration_seconds": 8.47,
      "text": "From what you've told me and what I found, this looks most like tonsillitis. We shouldn't forget a viral sore throat."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0041",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 316.4,
      "end_seconds": 317.77,
      "duration_seconds": 1.37,
      "text": "Is this permanent?"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0042",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 318.99,
      "end_seconds": 329.47,
      "duration_seconds": 10.48,
      "text": "I can't promise yet, but most people with tonsillitis do well once it's treated properly. We should do a throat swab for recurrent tonsillitis."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0043",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 331.26,
      "end_seconds": 333.98,
      "duration_seconds": 2.72,
      "text": "When would that take place?"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0044",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 335.07,
      "end_seconds": 341.72,
      "duration_seconds": 6.65,
      "text": "The treatment will be phenoxymethylpenicillin, 250 milligrams, four times a day, ten days. It's for tonsillitis."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0045",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 343.76,
      "end_seconds": 346.61,
      "duration_seconds": 2.85,
      "text": "Alright, I'll pick it up today."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0046",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 352.12,
      "end_seconds": 374.49,
      "duration_seconds": 22.37,
      "text": "Plenty of fluids and soft foods, and he can return to school when the fever has gone. A short walk every day, even twenty minutes, will help more than you'd think. We'll refer you to the ENT clinic. Let's review you if recurrent, tonsil review. That's everything on my side. Anything you're unsure about?"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0047",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 376.31,
      "end_seconds": 379.68,
      "duration_seconds": 3.37,
      "text": "I think I understand everything. Thanks."
    }
  ]
}